   "id": 90,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    1320
   ],
   "size": [
    900,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 38,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Agent slots",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Agent slots (Genobi fills these in the API JSON)\n\n**Text widgets**\n\n| slot | node id | input | default |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| base prompt | `4` CLIPTextEncode | `text` | cafe scene with a glass of iced coffee |\n| element name | `21` CLIPTextEncode (SAM 3.1) | `text` | `drink` |\n| instruction | `40` PrimitiveStringMultiline | `value` | `hold a banana instead of the drink` |\n\nSeeds: `7.seed` (base), `51.seed` (edit).\n\n**Optional images** (bypassed here, absent from the API JSON until Genobi adds them)\n\n| slot | node id | wiring when used |\n|---|---|---|\n| external base image | `10` LoadImage | `11.on_true = [\"10\", 0]` and `11.switch = true` |\n| reference image | `49` LoadImage | `50[\"images.image1\"] = [\"49\", 0]`; cite it as `<ref_image_1>` in the instruction |\n\nThe element name accepts SAM 3.1 syntax: `drink:2` keeps up to two detections.\n"
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 91,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    940,
    1320
   ],
   "size": [
    860,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 39,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How it works · open questions",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How the three stages connect\n\n1. **Base** — FLUX 3 Image Klein distilled, 1024 x 1024, 16 steps, cfg 1, euler / simple (the bundled template settings). The switch `11` lets stages 2 and 3 run on a loaded image instead; Klein then never runs.\n2. **Find** — SAM 3.1 (`SAM3_Detect`, core) segments the element named in `21`. The mask is grown 24 px, then blurred for a soft edge (`FeatherMask` only feathers the canvas border, so it is not used). The box goes out as `BOUNDING_BOX` and as a STRING via `PreviewAny`.\n3. **Swap** — the SAM box becomes a FLUX 3 layout element (`CreateBoundingBoxes` → `Flux3LayoutPrompt`), so the instruction is tied to `<obj_1>`. The base is `<ref_image_0>` in `ReferenceMultiLatent`, as in the official edit template. Klein regenerates the whole frame, so the result is composited back over the base through the feathered mask.\n\n**Open questions (need a GPU run)**: does Klein keep pixels outside `<obj_1>` well enough to skip the composite; is 24 px of growth enough for an object larger than the drink; does an empty SAM result (nothing found) need a guard. Details in `workflows/klein/README.md`.\n"
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
